  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 92b2c8003586277498a007ee213cc22b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 'Log - [unassigned 3]'
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FloppyData
  diskName: 'Log - [unassigned 3]'
  logTitle: Conflicting Readings
  author: '[Captain TBD]'
  shipName: '[Unassigned]'
  dateRecorded: '[TBD]'
  logText: 'I''ve been reviewing the latest survey data, and something isn''t adding
    up.

    The atmospheric readings from yesterday''s scan don''t match the ones
    I collected this morning. Oxygen concentration, surface pressure, even the estimated
    temperature. All different.

    Ordinarily, I''d assume the equipment was malfunctioning.
    But I ran the diagnostics twice, and everything came back within tolerance.

    The
    strangest part is that the orbital imagery hasn''t changed. Same cloud formations,
    same weather systems, same visible landmarks.

    I checked the original data
    files to make sure I hadn''t accidentally compared readings from two different
    planets.

    I hadn''t.

    SYS-CTRL reports no instrument faults.

    I''ll
    run another scan tomorrow and compare the results. If the discrepancy persists,
    I''ll have to mark the planet for further investigation.

    For now, I''m
    keeping both sets of readings. No sense discarding data just because I can''t
    explain it.'
